WEBVTT

00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:19,740
I've been on your ADK complete, so ADK complete is a vitamin A, vitamin D, vitamin K.

00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:25,900
I think there's some vitamin E in it too for a few months. It's all the fat soluble vitamins.

00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:33,660
As I was unable to get my vitamin D level up on another brand in the last two months, it has gone

00:00:33,660 --> 00:00:41,420
from 30 to 36, which is a big rise, with one pill a day. So one pill a day of the ADK complete is 5,000.

00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:47,340
I use vitamin D. I can't remember how much of the other supplements. The other vitamins

00:00:47,340 --> 00:00:54,780
it has in it, but should I double my dose or stay on the course? I would double the dose of that.

00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:00,380
Sometimes people need to be up 10, even 20,000. I use a vitamin D to get their vitamin D levels up,

00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:05,900
which brings up another question, why would a person have difficulty getting their vitamin D levels up?

00:01:06,540 --> 00:01:09,500
It can be multiple different reasons. It can be

00:01:10,460 --> 00:01:17,660
absorption issues. If you have a history of gallbladder issues, that can be

00:01:18,940 --> 00:01:24,860
you can have difficulty in absorbing your fat soluble vitamins. You can have a damaged gut

00:01:25,420 --> 00:01:35,180
causing issues in absorption of fat soluble nutrients. Probably the most common reason why a person

00:01:35,980 --> 00:01:41,580
has a sluggish ability to get their vitamin D levels up is that they have

00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:49,020
defects in their vitamin D receptor genes. So there are specific genes that help you absorb and

00:01:49,020 --> 00:01:53,580
utilize vitamin D. If you have a lot of defects in those genes, it can be more difficult to

00:01:53,580 --> 00:01:55,580
use. You just need to take more vitamin D.

